{# Shared price rendering for all 3 public layouts (standard/compact/grid) —
   used at both render sites (front + back of the flip card) in each. A
   simple product (no variants) renders as a single plain text price, byte-
   for-byte identical to before this macro existed — see the early return
   below, which still uses the raw ISO $currency code exactly as before,
   never $currencyDisplay. A product with variants renders one stacked row
   per price (label left/muted, price right, currency on every row) — see
   .price-stack/.price-row/.price-item-label/.price-item-value in each
   layout's own <style> block. $currencyDisplay is the symbol when exactly
   one supported currency uses it, otherwise the code — see
   MenuPreferencesResolver::getCurrencyDisplay(). See also
   Product::hasPriceVariants(). #}
{% macro price(product, currency, showCurrency, currencyDisplay) %}{% if product.hasPriceVariants %}<span class="price-stack"><span class="price-row">{% if product.basePriceLabel %}<span class="price-item-label">{{ product.basePriceLabel }}</span>{% endif %}<span class="price-item-value">{{ (product.convertedPrice / 100)|number_format(2) }}{% if showCurrency %} {{ currencyDisplay }}{% endif %}</span></span>{% for variant in product.priceVariants %}<span class="price-row"><span class="price-item-label">{{ variant.label }}</span><span class="price-item-value">{{ (product.getConvertedVariantPrice(variant) / 100)|number_format(2) }}{% if showCurrency %} {{ currencyDisplay }}{% endif %}</span></span>{% endfor %}</span>{% else %}{{ (product.convertedPrice / 100)|number_format(2) }}{% if showCurrency %} {{ currency }}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
